      "prompt": {
        "prompt": "You are implementing a contact point-person discovery module for the SBPS Supply Radar, a Python 3.11 project at /home/alex/Projects/SBPS.\n\nNOTE: Track A (site-based buyer matching) has already been implemented by a previous agent. The models.py file now includes DemandType, SiteType, DealStructure enums and new fields on Signal and BuyerDemand. Do NOT modify those.\n\n## Context\nThe radar discovers surplus power equipment and identifies the company that owns it. The critical gap: there's no mechanism to identify the specific HUMAN at that company who handles asset disposition. The system needs to infer likely role titles from the trigger event and query people-data APIs.\n\n## Your tasks — make ALL changes directly:\n\n### 1. Add config field (src/sbps/config.py)\nAdd after recap_api_token:\n    apollo_api_key: str = field(default_factory=lambda: os.getenv(\"APOLLO_API_KEY\", \"\"))\n\n### 2. Create src/sbps/contact_discovery.py\nFull module with:\n- TRIGGER_ROLE_MAP dict: keywords (bankrupt, chapter, retire, decommission, cancel, withdraw, dismiss, impair, sell, surplus, close, shut down) to role title lists\n- DEFAULT_ROLES list: Asset Disposition Manager, Director of Asset Management, Plant Manager, VP Operations, CFO\n- SOURCE_ROLE_HINTS dict: SignalSource to role lists (PACER to CRO/CFO/GC, EIA_RETIREMENT to Plant Manager/Asset Mgmt, etc.)\n- ContactCandidate dataclass: name, title, company, email, phone, linkedin_url, confidence, source, outreach_angle\n- DiscoveryResult dataclass: signal_id, company_name, inferred_roles, candidates, best_candidate, outreach_strategy\n- infer_roles(signal) -> list[str]: match trigger keywords, fall back to source hints, then defaults\n- build_outreach_angle(signal, role_title=\"\") -> str: trigger-specific messaging. Bankruptcy to speed/certainty. Retirement to before demolition. Cancellation to idle equipment. Impairment to balance sheet relief. Generic to SBPS transparent 1/1/1 differentiator. Always include company name.\n- search_apollo(company_name, role_titles, api_key) -> list[ContactCandidate]: POST to https://api.apollo.io/api/v1/people/search with X-Api-Key header, search top 3 roles, 5 per page. Return [] if no key.\n- rank_candidates(candidates, preferred_roles) -> sorted list by role match quality\n- ContactDiscovery class: discover(signal) and discover_batch(signals). Without API key to create inferred placeholders (empty name, source=\"inferred\").\n\n### 3. Integrate with call sheet (src/sbps/call_sheet.py)\nReplace _build_suggested_angle to delegate to contact_discovery.build_outreach_angle(signal, \"\"). Keep the rest of call sheet generation unchanged.\n\n### 4. Integrate into CLI (src/sbps/cli.py)\nAdd import ContactDiscovery. In _run_pipeline, after step 6 (buyer matching, where matched = match_signals_to_buyers(matched, buyers)), add step 6b: discover contacts. Code:\n    # 6b. Discover contacts\n    console.print(\"\\n[bold]6b. Discovering point-person contacts...[/bold]\")\n    discovery = ContactDiscovery(apollo_api_key=cfg.apollo_api_key)\n    discovery_results = await discovery.discover_batch(matched)\n    found_contacts = sum(1 for r in discovery_results if r.best_candidate)\n    console.print(f\" [green]✓ {found_contacts} signals have contact candidates[/green]\")\n\n### 5. Write tests (tests/test_contact_discovery.py)\nTest infer_roles (retirement/bankruptcy/cancellation/unknown/source hints), build_outreach_angle (bankruptcy/retirement/generic), rank_candidates, ContactDiscovery.discover (no API key, empty company), discover_batch. Use pytest-asyncio or asyncio.run for async tests.\n\n### 6. Ensure pytest-asyncio available\nRead pyproject.toml. If pytest-asyncio not in dev deps, add it to the [dev] extras. Add asyncio_mode = \"auto\" to [tool.pytest.ini_options] if missing. Install the dev extras: cd /home/alex/Projects/SBPS && pip install -e \".[dev]\" (or if .venv exists: .venv/bin/pip install -e \".[dev]\")\n\nIMPORTANT: Read each file BEFORE editing to confirm exact content. Use ctx_edit for all edits. After all edits, run: cd /home/alex/Projects/SBPS && .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_contact_discovery.py -v 2>&1 | tail -50"
